  "preamble": "Occlusion of the alveolar lateral approximant [l] to the plosive [t], keeping the alveolar closure but losing lateral airflow. In Khanty, Proto-Khanty *l (from Proto-Uralic *l and *δ) merged with the lateral fricative *ɬ in most dialects; the merged sound stays ɬ in Kazym and Surgut, is l in Obdorsk and the Far Eastern dialects (e.g. Vakh), and became t in the Middle Ob and Southern (Konda) dialects. Hence Proto-Uralic *kolme 'three' > Proto-Khanty *kɔlǝm > Middle Ob хутум, Konda хутәм, against Kazym хөԓәм and Vakh ӄоләм.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Occlusion, Fortition, Delateralization, Merger",
